      "writtenOn": "2021-07-16T03:56:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If for some reason the system_server calls the bindApplication() a bit late - and it\u0027s totally normal because there are often quite some lock contentions within the system_server - in this case the code in line 1138 would loop for quite some times and it wastes the cpu cycles for nothing. The cost of posting a message to a message queue won\u0027t be less than using a lock word - in fact the message queue\u0027s implementation itself involves locks. When there is http proxy update (which is the most common case here), a synchronized() lock word stays as a thin lock (refer: art/runtime/monitor.cc), its cost should be minimal. \n\nSo I\u0027d like to take lorenzo@\u0027s idea above into the account. Maybe put that code block around line 6707.",
